a590441fc3d"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:project.symbol-reference-completeness","usage":{"input_tokens":69651,"output_tokens":2427,"requests":4}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"3ef67c15876c42e80f753f0b9e8d52d994d5461b146218455e70760975862e99"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:G6","usage":{"input_tokens":340674,"output_tokens":7150,"requests":9}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State that the subprocess spawn helpers themselves (`_engine_run_env` ~:1535-1544 and `_engine_run_at` ~:518-524) construct their env via `child_env(...)` so the shim PYTHONPATH prefix reaches the child, not merely that the nine env_extra dict keys are renamed to REBAR_TEST_HLC_NOW.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.3161,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["_engine_run_env (test_concurrency_regression.py:1535-1544) is where env is built from _engine.engine_env and the subprocess is spawned; the nine :1585.. sites are only env_extra={...} dict args to it","_engine_run_at (:518-524) is the spawn point for the renamed :521 read","Plan: 'new child_env(...) prepends tests/_child_hooks_shim/ to PYTHONPATH' — the shim only runs when that prefix reaches the CHILD, i.e. when the spawn helper's env goes through child_env, not merely when a caller's dict key is renamed"],"finding":"For the subprocess HLC tests, the shim is only loaded if tests/_child_hooks_shim/ is on the CHILD interpreter's PYTHONPATH, which child_env sets. But the nine renamed sites (test_concurrency_regression.py:1585,1588,1589,1590,1606,1622,1663,1679,1697) are only dict literals passed as env_extra into the subprocess-spawning helper `_engine_run_env` (lines 1535-1544); `_engine_run_at` (lines 518-524) is the spawn point for :521. The plan says to rewire the sites 'through child_env' and rename the key, but does not state that `_engine_run_env`/`_engine_run_at` themselves build their env via child_env. If only the call-site dict keys are renamed to REBAR_TEST_HLC_NOW without routing the spawn helper's env through child_env (which prepends the shim PYTHONPATH), the child never runs the shim, _clock stays time.time_ns, and the injected clock is silently ignored.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f6d55a4969466d85c","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — subprocess tests bullet ('Rewire test_concurrency_regression.py:521 and the nine env_extra sites ... through child_env')","norm_id":"n2dbf89c485cd8185","priority":0.4839,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Executor renames the env_extra keys to REBAR_TEST_HLC_NOW but leaves _engine_run_env building env via _engine.engine_env without child_env — children spawn without the shim PYTHONPATH, _clock stays wall-clock, and the skew/scenario-A/scenario-B convergence assertions break or pass vacuously"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"In the Approach, specify that `_engine_run_env` and `_engine_run_at` wrap their constructed env with `child_env(env, hlc_now=...)` (which both prepends tests/_child_hooks_shim/ to PYTHONPATH and sets REBAR_TEST_HLC_NOW), so every child interpreter runs the rebinding sitecustomize; the nine call sites then only supply the hlc_now value.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7222,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"insufficient","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent